56;166;96m+7\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;179;89;107m-2\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 133 \u001b[22m - the site settings of the header and the footer (the notice in the top bar, the\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 134 \u001b[22m   opening hours, the note), because a site setting has one value for all languages\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 135 \u001b[22m - the filter \"Show only\" of the search, a record of the \"Search index\" folder\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[38;2;220;90;90m\u001b[48;2;61;1;0m 136 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- the search results: ke_search indexes a page translation only with content of                                                              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;220;90;90m 137 -\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  its own language, so the index holds no Kiswahili page yet                                                                                 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G \u001b[5G \u001b[2m 136 \u001b[12G\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 137 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mThe search in Kiswahili finds the Kiswahili pages by their title and by the English                                                          \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 138 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mcontent they show. ke_search writes an index entry for a page translation only                                                               \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 139 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mwhere it has content elements of its own; for a translation that falls back to                                                               \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 140 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mEnglish, `Classes/Search/IndexFallbackContentOfPageTranslations.php` (hook                                                                   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 141 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m`modifyPagesIndexEntry`) gives it the English content. The news are indexed in                                                               \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 142 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242mEnglish only and are not found from the Kiswahili search.                                                                                    \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 143 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m                                                                                                                                             \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 144 \u001b[22m ## Editors\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 145 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 146 \u001b[22m The setup creates the backend user group \"Editors\", after the import, on every\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  Allowed\u001b[14Gby a\u001b[19Gto mode\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[42;1H\u001b[40;3H\u001b[?25h"]
